ovember 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Michigan law sets out when a person occupying land can claim title by adverse possession, and how an owner can remove someone who has no right to be there.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Section 600.5801 is the Michigan limitation on actions to recover possession of land or make entry (time periods; special cases for defendants claiming under deed, court-ordered sale, tax deed or will). (MCL 600.5801 (title per Chapter 58 index); <a href='https://legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectName=mcl-236-1961-58' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A person who takes possession by forcible entry, holds by force after peaceable entry, or comes into possession by trespass without color of title or other possessory interest can be removed by summary proceedings. (MCL 600.5714(1)(f); <a href='https://www.legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectname=mcl-600-5714' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Michigan?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Michigan houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><h2>Michigan Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession FAQ</h2><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Can a squatter take ownership of my Michigan house?</h3><p> Check the statute and talk to a Michigan attorney about your facts.</p><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/michigan-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Michigan Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/michigan-eviction-notice/'>Michigan Eviction Notice: Types and Days</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/michigan-tax-deed-and-tax-lien-sales/'>Michigan Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/michigan-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Michigan guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-michigan/'>We buy houses in Michigan</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectName=mcl-236-1961-58' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>MCL 600.5801 (title per Chapter 58 index)</a></li><li><a href='https://www.legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectname=mcl-600-5714' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>MCL 600.5714(1)(f)</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Michigan Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can a squatter take ownership of my Michigan house?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Only by meeting every requirement of the adverse possession statute cited above for the full period. Check the statute and talk to a Michigan attorney about your facts.\"}}]}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Michigan\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-michigan/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Michigan Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/michigan-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Michigan Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession", "rank_math_description": "Michigan squatters rights and adverse possession: what the statutes say and how owners remove occupants or sell. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "michigan squatters rights"}, {"slug": "michigan-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights", "title": "Michigan Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: Rules for Selling a Rental", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inlin