argin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Michigan Eviction Notice Rules: Notice Types, Days and Selling the House</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Michigan</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Michigan Eviction Notice Rules: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Michigan Eviction Notice Rules sale</li><li>Turn the Michigan Eviction Notice Rules offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Michigan House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Michigan law requires a landlord to give a specific written notice before filing an eviction, and the number of days depends on the reason.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Nonpayment: landlord may terminate by written 7-day notice to quit. (MCL 554.134(2); <a href='https://www.legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectName=mcl-554-134' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Summary proceedings for nonpayment when tenant holds over 7 days after service of written demand for possession. (MCL 600.5714(1)(a); <a href='https://www.legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectName=mcl-600-5714' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Serious continuing health hazard or extensive physical damage: 7 days after demand to deliver up possession or substantially restore/repair. (MCL 600.5714(1)(d); <a href='https://www.legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectName=mcl-600-5714' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Controlled substance clause termination: 24-hour notice to quit (with formal police report); violence/threat of injury: 7-day notice to quit. (MCL 554.134(4); 600.5714(1)(b),(e); <a href='https://www.legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectName=mcl-600-5714' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Holdover after lease termination under a lease power, expiration of term, or notice to quit under MCL 554.134 supports summary proceedings; year-to-year tenancy terminated by notice to quit giving 1 year. (MCL 600.5714(1)(c); 554.134(3); <a href='https://www.legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectName=mcl-554-134' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Michigan?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Michigan houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/michigan-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/'>Michigan Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/michigan-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Michigan Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/michigan-tax-deed-and-tax-lien-sales/'>Michigan Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/michigan-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Michigan guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-michigan/'>We buy houses in Michigan</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://www.legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectName=mcl-554-134' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>MCL 554.134(2)</a></li><li><a href='https://www.legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectName=mcl-600-5714' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>MCL 600.5714(1)(a)</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Michigan Eviction Notice Rules, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Michigan\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-michigan/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Michigan Eviction Notice: Types and Days\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/michigan-eviction-notice/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Michigan Eviction Notice: Types and Days", "rank_math_description": "Michigan eviction notice rules: notice types, required days, which court hears the case and selling a rental. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "michigan eviction notice"}, {"slug": "michigan-tax-deed-and-tax-lien-sales", "title": "Michigan Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales: Process, Redemption and Selling First", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Michigan Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales: Process, Redemption and Selling First</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Michigan</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Michigan Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Michigan Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales sale</li><li>Turn the Michigan Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Michigan House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>When property tax goes unpaid in Michigan, the statutes allow the taxing authority to sell a lien or the property itself, and they give the owner a set time to redeem.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Michigan uses forfeiture and foreclosure: on March 1, property delinquent for the preceding 12 months or more is forfeited to the county treasurer. (MCL 211.78g(1); <a href='https://www.legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectName=mcl-211-78g' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A $175 fee is added to each forfeited property. (MCL 211.78g(1); <a href='https://www.legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectName=mcl-211-78g' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Redemption is allowed until the March 31 after entry of the foreclosure judgment (or 21 days after judgment in a contested case) by paying taxes, interest, penalties, fees. (MCL 211.78g(3); <a href='https://www.legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectName=mcl-211-78g' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Additional interest of 1/2% per month (noncompounded) on originally delinquent taxes, from the preceding March 1, applies on redemption. (MCL 211.78g(3)(b); <a href='https://www.legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectName=mcl-211-78g' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Absolute title and equity vest in the foreclosing governmental unit on the March 31 after judgment; persons with an interest may claim remaining proceeds after sale under section 78t. (MCL 211.78g(2); 2020 PA 256 note; <a href='https://www.legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectName=mcl-211-78g' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Michigan?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Michigan houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/michigan-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/'>Michigan Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/michigan-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Michigan Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/michigan-eviction-notice/'>Michigan Eviction Notice: Types and Days</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/michigan-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Michigan guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-michigan/'>We buy houses in Michigan</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://www.legislature.mi.gov/Laws/MCL?objectName=mcl-211-78g' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>MCL 211.78g(1)</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Michigan Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Michigan\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-michigan/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Michigan Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/michigan-tax-deed-and-tax-lien-sales/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Michigan Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales", "rank_math_description": "Michigan tax deed and tax lien sales: who runs the sale, interest, redemption periods and selling before the sale. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "michigan tax deed sales"}]